{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_qtfbrma3x4keleny4tzltr3vuzzeumpe6tu5bqu5d2x5r4iogtvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01WVA2hPmBsLa1EGdG15vhxp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust/TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md","content":"# libpng C -> Rust translation contract (READ THIS FIRST)\n\nYou are translating one C file (or a range of functions from one C file) of\nlibpng 1.6.59 from `c_src/src/*.c` into a Rust module in `src/`.\n\nThe goal is a **mechanical, line-by-line transliteration** that behaves\n*identically* to the C, not idiomatic Rust. Do NOT restructure, do NOT \"fix\"\nbugs, do NOT change the order of checks, do NOT change error messages.\n\n## 0. Foundation already written (DO NOT MODIFY THESE FILES)\n\n| file | contents |\n|---|---|\n| `src/types.rs` | all `png_*` type aliases, public structs (`png_color`, `png_color_16`, `png_color_8`, `png_sPLT_entry`, `png_sPLT_t`, `png_text`, `png_time`, `png_unknown_chunk`, `png_row_info`, `png_xy`, `png_XYZ`, `png_image`, `png_control`, `png_compression_buffer`, `jmp_buf`), all callback types |\n| `src/pngstruct.rs` | `png_struct` (all fields, same names as pngstruct.h) |\n| `src/pnginfo.rs` | `png_info` (all fields, same names as pnginfo.h) |\n| `src/pngpriv.rs` | every `#define` constant from pngpriv.h / png.h / pnglibconf.h, plus macro-equivalent inline fns |\n| `src/zlib.rs` | `z_stream` + `inflate*`/`deflate*`/`crc32` (zlib API subset), `Z_*` constants |\n| `src/pngerror.rs` | pngerror.c (done) |\n| `src/pngmem.rs` | pngmem.c (done) |\n| `src/pngrio.rs` | pngrio.c (done) |\n| `src/pngwio.rs` | pngwio.c (done) |\n\nRead the files you need before writing code. `src/pngrio.rs`, `src/pngmem.rs`\nand `src/pngerror.rs` show the exact expected style.\n\n## 1. Rules for exported symbols\n\nEvery function that the C file defines **without** `static` must become:\n\n```rust\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn png_whatever(a: png_structrp, b: c_int) -> c_int { ... }\n```\n\n* Use `extern \"C-unwind\"` (NOT `extern \"C\"`) everywhere — the crate relies on\n  unwinding for the simplified-API error path.\n* `static` C functions become `pub(crate) unsafe fn name(...)` (plain Rust ABI)\n  **unless** they are used as a C callback / function pointer stored in a\n  struct, in which case they must also be `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` (but\n  without `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`).\n* Functions declared `PNG_NORETURN` in C (`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`,\n  `png_longjmp`, `png_fixed_error`) return `!` in Rust. Calling them diverges.\n\n## 2. Type mapping\n\n| C | Rust |\n|---|---|\n| `int`, `unsigned int` | `c_int`, `c_uint` |\n| `png_byte` | `png_byte` (= `u8`) |\n| `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` | `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` |\n| `png_uint_32` / `png_int_32` | `png_uint_32` (=`u32`) / `png_int_32` (=`i32`) |\n| `png_fixed_point` | `png_fixed_point` (= `i32`) |\n| `size_t`, `png_alloc_size_t` | `usize`, `png_alloc_size_t` (= `usize`) |\n| `double` | `f64` |\n| `char *` / `const char *` | `png_charp` / `png_const_charp` |\n| `png_structrp`, `png_const_structrp`, `png_structp` | all `*mut png_struct` (aliases exist) |\n| `png_inforp`, `png_const_inforp`, `png_infop` | all `*mut png_info` (aliases exist) |\n| `png_bytep` / `png_const_bytep` | `*mut u8` / `*const u8` |\n| `uInt` (zlib) | `u32` |\n| `voidpf` (zlib) | `*mut c_void` |\n| `FILE *` | `*mut libc::FILE` |\n| function pointer typedefs | the `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(...)>` aliases in `types.rs` |\n\n`const` is dropped on struct pointers (ABI identical), so no casts are needed.\n\n## 3. Idioms\n\n* String literals: `c\"some text\".as_ptr()` produces a `*const c_char`.\n* NULL: `core::ptr::null()` / `core::ptr::null_mut()`.\n* `p != NULL` -> `!p.is_null()`; `p == NULL` -> `p.is_null()`.\n* `fn_ptr != NULL` -> `f.is_some()`; call with `if let Some(f) = (*png_ptr).read_data_fn { f(..) }`.\n* `->` becomes `(*ptr).field`.\n* Pointer arithmetic: `p + n` -> `p.add(n)`, `p - n` -> `p.sub(n)`,\n  `*p++ = v` -> `*p = v; p = p.add(1);`, `*--p = v` -> `p = p.sub(1); *p = v;`.\n* Pointer difference `a - b` -> `(a as usize) - (b as usize)` (or\n  `a.offset_from(b)` when a real element count is wanted).\n* `memcpy`/`memset`/`memmove`/`memcmp`/`strlen`/`strcmp` — use the helpers in\n  `crate::pngpriv` (`memcpy(dst, src, n)` etc., all take `*mut u8`/`*const u8`;\n  cast with `as *mut u8` / `as *const u8`).\n* Arithmetic **must not panic**: C integer arithmetic wraps. Use\n  `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` / `wrapping_mul` when a value could overflow,\n  and be careful with `as` casts (Rust `as` truncates like C).\n* Beware of C integer promotion: `(png_byte)a - (png_byte)b` is computed in\n  `int` in C. Translate as `a as c_int - b as c_int`.\n* Local arrays: `let mut buf: [u8; N] = [0; N];` then `buf.as_mut_ptr()`.\n* `switch` -> `match` (remember C fall-through must be replicated explicitly).\n* `goto` -> restructure with a labelled `loop`/`break` or duplicate the code;\n  keep semantics identical.\n* Do **not** use `Box`, `Vec`, `String` or any `Drop` type for locals in\n  functions that may call `png_error` (a real `longjmp` may fly past them).\n  Use raw pointers + `png_malloc`/`png_free` exactly like the C code.\n\n## 4. Cross-module references\n\nEverything is a flat set of modules under `crate::`. Import what you need, e.g.\n\n```rust\nuse core::ffi::{c_char, c_int, c_uint, c_void};\nuse crate::pngpriv::*;\nuse crate::pngstruct::*;\nuse crate::pnginfo::*;\nuse crate::types::*;\nuse crate::zlib::*;\nuse crate::pngerror::{png_error, png_warning, png_benign_error, png_app_error,\n    png_app_warning, png_chunk_error, png_chunk_warning, png_chunk_benign_error,\n    png_chunk_report, png_safecat, png_format_number, png_warning_parameter,\n    png_warning_parameter_unsigned, png_warning_parameter_signed,\n    png_formatted_warning, png_fixed_error, png_longjmp, png_safe_execute,\n    png_safe_error, png_safe_warning};\nuse crate::pngmem::{png_malloc, png_malloc_warn, png_malloc_base, png_calloc,\n    png_free, png_malloc_array, png_realloc_array, png_destroy_png_struct};\n```\n\nThe module for each C file is named after it: `png.c` -> `crate::png`,\n`pngrutil.c` -> `crate::pngrutil`, etc.\n\n### `PNG_WARNING_PARAMETERS(p)` / `png_warning_parameters`\n\n`png_warning_parameters p;` becomes\n\n```rust\nlet mut p: [[c_char; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT] =\n    [[0; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT];\n```\n\nand is passed as `p.as_mut_ptr()` (type `*mut [c_char; 32]`).\n\n### zlib\n\n`png_ptr->zstream` is a `crate::zlib::z_stream` with fields `next_in`\n(`*const u8`), `avail_in` (`u32`), `next_out` (`*mut u8`), `avail_out` (`u32`),\n`msg` (`*const c_char`), `zalloc`, `zfree`, `opaque`, `state`, `total_in`,\n`total_out`, `adler`, `data_type`, `reserved`.\n\nCall the zlib functions as free functions:\n`inflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, wb)`, `inflate(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, flush)`,\n`inflateReset2`, `inflateReset`, `inflateValidate`, `inflateEnd`,\n`deflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, level, method, wb, memLevel, strategy)`,\n`deflate`, `deflateReset`, `deflateEnd`, `crc32(crc, ptr, len)`.\n`ZLIB_VERNUM` is 0x12b0 (>= 0x1240), so compile the \"modern zlib\" branches.\n`PNGZ_MSG_CAST(s)` is just `s`; `PNGZ_INPUT_CAST(b)` is just `b`.\n`ZLIB_IO_MAX` is `crate::zlib::ZLIB_IO_MAX` (`u32::MAX`).\n\n### `png_debug*`\n\nAll `png_debug`, `png_debug1`, `png_debug2` calls are no-ops — just delete them.\n\n### `PNG_UNUSED(x)`\n\nDelete.\n\n## 5. Which `#ifdef`s are ON\n\nTreat these as **defined** (see `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h` for the full list —\nessentially everything except the CPU-specific optimizations):\n\n* All `PNG_READ_*`, `PNG_WRITE_*`, chunk support, `PNG_SETJMP_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_POINT_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_FIXED_POINT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONSOLE_IO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_PROGRESSIVE_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SEQUENTIAL_READ_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_COLORSPACE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GAMMA_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WARNINGS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ERROR_TEXT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_TEXT_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_TIME_RFC1123_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONVERT_tIME_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_EASY_ACCESS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_INCH_CONVERSIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SET_OPTION_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` (+ READ/WRITE/SET/STORE/SAVE variants),\n  `PNG_USER_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GET_PALETTE_MAX_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_INFO_IMAGE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_POINTER_INDEXING_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BUILD_GRAYSCALE_PALETTE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_COMPOSITE_NODIV_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_USE_READ_MACROS`, `PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_FORMAT_AFIRST_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_*_BGR/AFIRST/STDIO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SAVE_INT_32_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_TRANSFORM_*`.\n\nTreat these as **NOT defined** (omit the code entirely):\n\n* `PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K`, `PNG_ARM_NEON_*`, `PNG_MIPS_*`, `PNG_POWERPC_*`,\n  `PNG_LOONGARCH_*`, `PNG_INTEL_SSE`, `PNG