**defined** (see `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h` for the full list —\nessentially everything except the CPU-specific optimizations):\n\n* All `PNG_READ_*`, `PNG_WRITE_*`, chunk support, `PNG_SETJMP_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_POINT_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_FIXED_POINT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONSOLE_IO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_PROGRESSIVE_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SEQUENTIAL_READ_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_COLORSPACE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GAMMA_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WARNINGS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ERROR_TEXT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_TEXT_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_TIME_RFC1123_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONVERT_tIME_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_EASY_ACCESS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_INCH_CONVERSIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SET_OPTION_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` (+ READ/WRITE/SET/STORE/SAVE variants),\n  `PNG_USER_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GET_PALETTE_MAX_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_INFO_IMAGE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_POINTER_INDEXING_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BUILD_GRAYSCALE_PALETTE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_COMPOSITE_NODIV_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_USE_READ_MACROS`, `PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_FORMAT_AFIRST_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_*_BGR/AFIRST/STDIO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_SAVE_INT_32_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_WRITE_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_TRANSFORM_*`.\n\nTreat these as **NOT defined** (omit the code entirely):\n\n* `PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED`,\n  `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K`, `PNG_ARM_NEON_*`, `PNG_MIPS_*`, `PNG_POWERPC_*`,\n  `PNG_LOONGARCH_*`, `PNG_INTEL_SSE`, `PNG_RISCV_*`, `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS`,\n  `PNG_ARM_NEON_IMPLEMENTATION`, `PNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION`,\n  `PNG_USER_CONFIG`, `PNG_PREFIX`, `PNG_READ_QUANTIZE_SUPPORTED` is **ON**,\n  `PNG_READ_OPT_PLTE_SUPPORTED` is **ON**.\n* `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is **false** (`PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE` == BETA == 2\n  which is `< PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC` == 3), so inside\n  `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD ... #else ... #endif` you must take the **`#else`**\n  branch, and `#if !PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` code IS compiled.\n* `PNG_LIBPNG_VER < 10700` is **true**.\n* `PNG_ARM_NEON_OPT`, `PNG_INTEL_SSE_IMPLEMENTATION`, etc. are all `0`.\n\n## 6. Verification\n\nAfter writing the file, run\n\n```\ncargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\n\nOther modules may not exist yet, so unresolved-import errors from *other*\nmodules are expected; make sure there are **no errors in your own file**\n(you can check with `cargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | grep -c \"src/YOURFILE.rs\"`).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
