{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8afd9b59d97ce476","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VocSgoor1KhHBLAhfcUgs2","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-translate-bpUWKO-translated-rust/a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204/tasks/a8afd9b59d97ce476.output","summary":"Translation complete.\n\n## What was done\n\nWrote the full translation of `c_src/src/pngwtran.c` (574 lines) into `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust/src/pngwtran.rs` (610 lines), replacing the stub. No other file in the real crate was touched.\n\nSymbols:\n- `png_do_write_transformations` — the only `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn`\n- `png_do_pack`, `png_do_shift`, `png_do_write_swap_alpha`, `png_do_write_invert_alpha` — `pub(crate) unsafe fn` (plain Rust ABI, no `no_mangle`)\n\nAll `#ifdef`s taken as enabled per `pnglibconf.h` (verified: `PNG_WRITE_16BIT/PACK/PACKSWAP/SHIFT/SWAP/SWAP_ALPHA/INVERT_ALPHA/INVERT/BGR/FILLER/USER_TRANSFORM_SUPPORTED` all defined), so every branch of the C file is present.\n\nTranslation details worth noting:\n- `png_get_uint_16(bp)` maps to `PNG_get_uint_16` from `pngpriv.rs` (`PNG_USE_READ_MACROS` is on, and png.h aliases the lowercase name to the macro).\n- C integer promotion preserved: `row_info->bit_depth - bit_depth->red` → `as c_int` on both sides; `(value << shift)` → `(value as c_int) << shift` (shift kept as `c_uint`); `255 - *(sp++)` → `(255 - *sp as c_int) as png_byte`.\n- `!(png_ptr->flags & PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER)` → `(((*png_ptr).flags & PNG_FLAG_FILLER_AFTER) == 0) as c_int`.\n- The pointer-aliasing quirks in `png_do_write_invert_alpha` (`sp+=3; dp = sp; *dp = 255 - *(sp++)`) are reproduced literally with read-before-write ordering.\n- Multiplications that can overflow use `wrapping_mul` (`bit_depth * channels`, `channels * width`); loop counters use `wrapping_add`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Errors reported for `src/pngwtran.rs`: **none**.\n- `grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/pngwtran.rs` → **1**.\n- Full type-check was done in a throwaway `$TMPDIR` copy of the crate with stub definitions for the not-yet-translated png.c symbols (`png_image_free`, `png_muldiv`, `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_check_IHDR`, `png_fixed`); the whole crate compiled cleanly there with zero errors and zero warnings in `pngwtran.rs`.\n- Additionally ran a differential test in the scratch copy: exported thin C wrappers around the four Rust helpers, compiled a C harness containing verbatim copies of the original `static` functions from `pngwtran.c`, and compared `row_info` plus a 512-byte row buffer over 4134 cases (all `bit_depth`/`true bit_depth`/color-type/width combinations plus randomized data, including the low-bit-depth mask paths for `gray==1,bd==2` and `bd==4,gray==3`). Result: `cases=4134 failures=0`. The scratch copy has been deleted.\n\nRemaining crate-level errors are all pre-existing and belong to the not-yet-written `png.c`:\n```\nsrc/pngerror.rs:7    unresolved import crate::png::png_image_free\nsrc/pngget.rs:211,286,329   png_muldiv\nsrc/pngget.rs:526,580       png_XYZ_from_xy\nsrc/pngget.rs:1027          png_check_IHDR\nsrc/pngget.rs:1115,1120     png_fixed\n```","usage":{"total_tokens":117741,"tool_uses":28,"duration_ms":364607},"uuid":"4d994f64-5b1b-4162-b69d-8bddf1a70c61","session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204"}
