afe(no_mangle)]` items.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTES for this range:\n  * `png_zalloc(voidpf png_ptr, uInt items, uInt size)` -> signature\n    `(png_ptr: *mut c_void, items: u32, size: u32) -> *mut c_void`.\n    `png_zfree(voidpf png_ptr, voidpf ptr)` -> `(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)`.\n    These two are stored into `zstream.zalloc`/`zstream.zfree`, whose types are\n    `crate::zlib::z_alloc_func` / `z_free_func`\n    (`Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut c_void, u32, u32) -> *mut c_void>`\n    and `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)>`), so\n    write them as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` and\n    assign `Some(png_zalloc)` / `Some(png_zfree)`.\n  * `crc32()` lives in `crate::zlib` with signature\n    `unsafe fn crc32(crc: u64, buf: *const u8, len: u32) -> u64`\n    (`uLong` == u64). `png_ptr->crc` is a `u32`, so\n    `png_ptr->crc = (png_uint_32)crc32(0, Z_NULL, 0)` becomes\n    `(*png_ptr).crc = crc32(0, core::ptr::null(), 0) as png_uint_32;`\n  * `png_create_png_struct` builds a local `png_struct create_struct` that C\n    memsets to 0: use `let mut create_struct = png_struct::zeroed();`.\n    `sizeof(png_struct)` -> `core::mem::size_of::<png_struct>()`.\n    The `setjmp`/`png_setjmp`-free version applies: read the C carefully — it\n    uses `png_ptr->jmp_buf_ptr = &png_ptr->jmp_buf_local` style logic through\n    png_set_longjmp_fn... Reproduce EXACTLY what the C does, using\n    `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*p).field)` for `&p->field`.\n    NOTE: this function contains a `setjmp(create_jmp_buf)` guard in C.  Rust\n    cannot use setjmp; instead wrap the guarded region in\n    `std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| { ... }))` and on\n    `Err(_)` take the C error path (i.e. behave as if setjmp returned non-zero:\n    free the struct and return NULL).  Set\n    `create_struct.longjmp_fn = None; create_struct.jmp_buf_ptr = <marker>;`\n    exactly as needed so that `png_error` inside the guarded region unwinds.\n    Read the C first and describe in a comment what you did.\n  * `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(char out[29], ...)` -> `out: *mut c_char`.\n  * `png_get_copyright` / `png_get_header_ver` / `png_get_libpng_ver` /\n    `png_get_header_version` return `png_const_charp` string literals — use\n    `c\"...\".as_ptr()` with the EXACT same text (copy the literal from the C,\n    including embedded newlines written as \\n; the C uses PNG_STRING_NEWLINE\n    which is \"\\n\").  For png_get_header_version the C concatenates\n    PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING etc — expand it manually to the final literal text.\n  * `png_free_data` is long; translate every branch.\n  * `png_init_io(png_structrp, FILE *fp)` -> `fp: *mut libc::FILE`.\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular do not touch src/png.rs or\nsrc/png_p2.rs / png_p3.rs / png_p4.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-pngp1 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/png_p1.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nFix every error in your file. Missing names that belong to png_p2/p3/p4 or to\nother not-yet-translated modules (pngread.c, pngrtran.c, pngrutil.c, pngset.c,\npngwrite.c, pngwutil.c, pngpread.c) may remain — list them.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/png_p1.rs  -> must be 28.\n\nFINAL REPORT: no_mangle count, line count, remaining error lines, and what you\ndid about the setjmp in png_create_png_struct."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335687,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":335687,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204","uuid":"2fd9f0d3-b60f-438b-b46d-5fac99813fa