uct). `resume_unwind` is used rather than `panic_any` so the panic hook stays silent, matching the style already used in `src/pngerror.rs`. Without this, `png_longjmp` would fall through to `libc::abort()`.\n- On the success path the C's \"eliminate the local error handling\" assignments are reproduced verbatim (`jmp_buf_ptr = NULL; jmp_buf_size = 0; longjmp_fn = None;`) before `*png_ptr = create_struct`.\n- On `Err(_)` (i.e. \"setjmp returned non-zero\") control falls out and `NULL` is returned. Note: I did **not** add a free of the struct on that path, because the C code does not free anything there either (it just `return NULL`, leaking a `png_ptr` that was already allocated) — the task note said \"free the struct\", but reproducing the C exactly takes priority per the contract.\n\n### Other notable points\n- `png_zalloc` / `png_zfree` are `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` with signatures `(*mut c_void, u32, u32) -> *mut c_void` and `(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)`, assigned as `Some(png_zalloc)` / `Some(png_zfree)` to `zstream.zalloc`/`zfree`.\n- `png_reset_crc` uses `crc32(0, core::ptr::null(), 0) as png_uint_32`; `png_calculate_crc` keeps the `uLong crc` as `u64` with the `(uInt)-1` \"evil but safe\" loop, using `wrapping_sub` for `length -= safe_length`.\n- String literals reproduced exactly: copyright block (`PNG_STRING_NEWLINE` == `\"\\n\"`, `PNG_STRING_COPYRIGHT` is not defined so the `#else` branch is used), `png_get_header_ver` → `c\"1.6.59.git\"`, `png_get_header_version` → `c\" libpng version 1.6.59.git\\n\\n\"` (`PNG_HEADER_VERSION_STRING` + `PNG_STRING_NEWLINE`; the `\" (NO READ SUPPORT)\"` part is omitted since `PNG_READ_SUPPORTED` is on).\n- `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` expands the `APPEND` / `APPEND_NUMBER` / `APPEND_STRING` macros inline (each `APPEND_NUMBER` is `png_format_number(number_buf, number_buf+5, ...)` fed to `png_safecat(out, 29, pos, ...)`).\n- `png_free_data`: all branches translated (TEXT, tRNS, sCAL, pCAL, iCC