t_libpng_ver, png_get_header_ver, png_get_header_version,\n  png_build_grayscale_palette, png_handle_as_unknown,\n  png_chunk_unknown_handling, png_reset_zstream, png_access_version_number,\n  png_zstream_error\n\nALL of these are non-static in C, so ALL get\n`#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn <name>(...)`\n=> exactly 28 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` items.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTES for this range:\n  * `png_zalloc(voidpf png_ptr, uInt items, uInt size)` -> signature\n    `(png_ptr: *mut c_void, items: u32, size: u32) -> *mut c_void`.\n    `png_zfree(voidpf png_ptr, voidpf ptr)` -> `(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)`.\n    These two are stored into `zstream.zalloc`/`zstream.zfree`, whose types are\n    `crate::zlib::z_alloc_func` / `z_free_func`\n    (`Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut c_void, u32, u32) -> *mut c_void>`\n    and `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)>`), so\n    write them as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` and\n    assign `Some(png_zalloc)` / `Some(png_zfree)`.\n  * `crc32()` lives in `crate::zlib` with signature\n    `unsafe fn crc32(crc: u64, buf: *const u8, len: u32) -> u64`\n    (`uLong` == u64). `png_ptr->crc` is a `u32`, so\n    `png_ptr->crc = (png_uint_32)crc32(0, Z_NULL, 0)` becomes\n    `(*png_ptr).crc = crc32(0, core::ptr::null(), 0) as png_uint_32;`\n  * `png_create_png_struct` builds a local `png_struct create_struct` that C\n    memsets to 0: use `let mut create_struct = png_struct::zeroed();`.\n    `sizeof(png_struct)` -> `core::mem::size_of::<png_struct>()`.\n    The `setjmp`/`png_setjmp`-free version applies: read the C carefully — it\n    uses `png_ptr->jmp_buf_ptr = &png_ptr->jmp_buf_local` style logic through\n    png_set_longjmp_fn... Reproduce EXACTLY what the C does, using\n    `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!((*p).field)` for `&p->field`.\n    NOTE: this function contains a `setjmp(create_jmp_buf)` guard in C.  Rust\n    cannot use setjmp; instead wrap the guarded region in\n    `std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| { ... }))` and on\n    `Err(_)` take the C error path (i.e. behave as if setjmp returned non-zero:\n    free the struct and return NULL).  Set\n    `create_struct.longjmp_fn = None; create_struct.jmp_buf_ptr = <marker>;`\n    exactly as needed so that `png_error` inside the guarded region unwinds.\n    Read the C first and describe in a comment what you did.\n  * `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer(char out[29], ...)` -> `out: *mut c_char`.\n  * `png_get_copyright` / `png_get_header_ver` / `png_get_libpng_ver` /\n    `png_get_header_version` return `png_const_charp` string literals — use\n    `c\"...\".as_ptr()` with the EXACT same text (copy the literal from the C,\n    including embedded newlines written as \\n; the C uses PNG_STRING_NEWLINE\n    which is \"\\n\").  For png_get_header_version the C concatenates\n    PNG_LIBPNG_VER_STRING etc — expand it manually to the final literal text.\n  * `png_free_data` is long; translate every branch.\n  * `png_init_io(png_structrp, FILE *fp)` -> `fp: *mut libc::FILE`.\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular do not touch src/png.rs or\nsrc/png_p2.rs / png_p3.rs / png_p4.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-pngp1 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/png_p1.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nFix every error in your file. Missing names that belong to png_p2/p3/p4 or to\nother not-yet-translated modules (pngread.c, pngrtran.c, pngrutil.c, pngset.c,\npngwrite.c, pngwutil.c, pngpread.c) may remain — list them.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/png_p1.rs  -> must be 28.\n\nFINAL REPORT: no_mangle count, line count, remaining error lines, and what you\ndid about the setjmp in png_create_png_struct.","agentId":"a194da0649ab43bbe","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete.\n\n## Report\n\n**File written:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust/src/png_p1.rs`\n\n- **`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` count: 28** (exactly the 28 non-static functions in `c_src/src/png.c` lines 1..1067, in source order)\n- **Line count: 1122**\n- **Remaining error lines in `src/png_p1.rs`: 1**\n  - `src/png_p1.rs:719:5: error[E0425]: cannot find function png_save_uint_32` — belongs to `pngwutil.c` (not yet translated). This is the only unresolved name from my file.\n  - All other build errors are in other files (`src/pngerror.rs` → `png_image_free` from png_p4; `src/pngget.rs` → `png_muldiv`, `png_XYZ_from_xy`, `png_check_IHDR`, `png_fixed`, all from png_p2/p3/p4). No warnings are emitted for `png_p1.rs`.\n\n### What I did about the `setjmp` in `png_create_png_struct`\nThe C code wraps the struct-building region in `if (!setjmp(create_jmp_buf)) { ... }` and installs `&create_jmp_buf` / `longjmp` into `create_struct.jmp_buf_ptr` / `longjmp_fn` so that a `png_error` raised while building (e.g. from a broken application allocator, or from `png_user_version_check`'s warning path) returns `NULL` out of the function.\n\nRust translation (documented in a comment in the function):\n- The guarded region is a closure inside `std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(...))`.\n- `create_struct.jmp_buf_ptr` is still set to `core::ptr::addr_of_mut!(create_jmp_buf)` (a real, zeroed local `jmp_buf`) so it is non-NULL — `png_longjmp` only invokes `longjmp_fn` when `jmp_buf_ptr != NULL`. The buffer contents are never used.\n- `create_struct.longjmp_fn = Some(png_create_struct_longjmp)`, a new **non-exported** `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(*mut jmp_buf, c_int)` helper that does `std::panic::resume_unwind(Box::new(PngCreateStructUnwind))` (a private unit struct). `resume_unwind` is used rather than `panic_any` so the panic hook stays silent, matching the style already used in `src/pngerror.rs`. Without this, `png_longjmp` would fall through to `libc::abort()`.\n- On the success path the C's \"eliminate the local error handling\" assignments are reproduced verbatim (`jmp_buf_ptr = NULL; jmp_buf_size = 0; longjmp_fn = None;`) before `*png_ptr = create_struct`.\n- On `Err(_)` (i.e. \"setjmp returned non-zero\") control falls out and `NULL` is returned. Note: I did **not** add a free of the struct on that path, because the C code does not free anything there either (it just `return NULL`, leaking a `png_ptr` that was already allocated) — the task note said \"free the struct\", but reproducing the C exactly takes priority per the contract.\n\n### Other notable points\n- `png_zalloc` / `png_zfree` are `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` with signatures `(*mut c_void, u32, u32) -> *mut c_void` and `(*mut c_void, *mut c_void)`, assigned as `Some(png_zalloc)` / `Some(png_zfree)` to `zstream.zalloc`/`zfree`.\n- `png_reset_crc` uses `crc32(0, core::ptr::null(), 0) as png_uint_32`; `png_calculate_crc` keeps the `uLong crc` as `u64` with the `(uInt)-1` \"evil but safe\" loop, using `wrapping_sub` for `length -= safe_length`.\n- String literals reproduced exactly: copyright block (`PNG_STRING_NEWLINE` == `\"\\n\"`, `PNG_STRING_COPYRIGHT` is not defined so the `#else` branch is used), `png_get_header_ver` → `c\"1.6.59.git\"`, `png_get_header_version` → `c\" libpng version 1.6.59.git\\n\\n\"` (`PNG_HEADER_VERSION_STRING` + `PNG_STRING_NEWLINE`; the `\" (NO READ SUPPORT)\"` part is omitted since `PNG_READ_SUPPORTED` is on).\n- `png_convert_to_rfc1123_buffer` expands the `APPEND` / `APPEND_NUMBER` / `APPEND_STRING` macros inline (each `APPEND_NUMBER` is `png_format_number(number_buf, number_buf+5, ...)` fed to `png_safecat(out, 29, pos, ...)`).\n- `png_free_data`: all branches translated (TEXT, tRNS, sCAL, pCAL, iCCP, sPLT, unknown chunks, eXIf, hIST, PLTE, ROWS, plus the trailing `PNG_FREE_MUL` masking) — every relevant `*_SUPPORTED` macro is on in `pnglibconf.h`.\n- `png_handle_as_unknown` uses `num_chunk_list.wrapping_mul(5)` so the pointer offset computation can never panic."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":416789,"totalTokens":141789,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":139295,"output_tokens":2168,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":281},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":324},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":12,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":11,"editFileCount":2,"linesAdded":1124,"linesRemoved":1,"otherToolCount":0}}}
