.rs`**. `nm` on the resulting `libpng.so` confirmed all 6 symbols exported. Scratch copy deleted.\n\n**Notable translation decisions:**\n- `png_get_uint_32(p)` → `PNG_get_uint_32(p)` (read-macros build), per instructions.\n- `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` expands to `(*png_ptr).user_chunk_malloc_max` (`PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED` is on); the `png_uint_32` vs `size_t` comparison is done after casting `profile_length` to `png_alloc_size_t`, matching C's integer promotion.\n- `png_has_chunk(png_ptr, X)` expanded inline to `((*png_ptr).chunks & png_chunk_flag_from_index(PNG_INDEX_X)) != 0` (no `png_file_has_chunk` helper exists in `pngpriv.rs`). All of mDCV/sRGB/cHRM read support is on, so `check_chromaticities` == 1 and the full `png_set_rgb_coefficients` body is compiled.\n- Arguments containing `png_fp_sub(left, right, &error)` inside `png_muldiv(...)` calls were hoisted into named locals (`divisor`, `divisor2`, `inner`) to preserve the C evaluation-before-call semantics; the `error` accumulator ordering is unaffected because `png_fp_sub` only ever sets it to 1.\n- `132+12*temp` uses `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` to reproduce C unsigned-int wrap semantics; `profile_length - tag_start` uses `wrapping_sub` (short-circuit guarantees no wrap).\n- In `png_icc_profile_error` the two `message[pos++] = ...` writes use raw-pointer writes rather than Rust indexing so no bounds-check panic can be introduced (pos maxes out at 98 of 196 in practice, but the C write is unchecked).\n- `PNG_UNUSED(pos)` and `(void)` casts dropped; `png_debug*` — none present in this range. `PNG_WARNING_PARAMETERS` is not used anywhere in this range.\n\n**One thing for whoever translates `png_p3`:** png.c line 2130 defines a *macro* `#define png_fp_add(state, flags) ((state) |= (flags))` that shadows the static function I translated here. That later code must be inlined as `state |= flags` — it must NOT define a function named `png_fp_add`, or it will collide with the `pub(crate) fn png_fp_add` in `png_