","timestamp":"2026-08-22T14:34:15.994Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are translating part of libpng 1.6.59 from C to Rust.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — read completely before writing code:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the contract; follow it exactly)\n- src/types.rs, src/pngstruct.rs, src/pnginfo.rs, src/pngpriv.rs\n- src/png_p1.rs and src/png_p2.rs (already-translated sibling parts, same module, same style)\n- src/png.rs (the wrapper that `include!`s your file)\n\nSTEP 2 — read lines 1961..2999 of c_src/src/png.c (use Read with offset/limit).\n\nSTEP 3 — write the translation of THAT RANGE ONLY into src/png_p3.rs.\nIt is `include!`d into module `crate::png`, so:\n  * first line must be a plain `//` comment (never `//!`)\n  * no `#![...]` inner attributes\n\nContents of this range (in order):\n  png_check_IHDR       (EXPORTED)\n  png_check_fp_number  (EXPORTED)\n  png_check_fp_string  (EXPORTED)\n  png_pow10            (static)\n  png_ascii_from_fp    (EXPORTED)\n  png_ascii_from_fixed (EXPORTED)\n  png_fixed            (EXPORTED)\n  png_fixed_ITU        (EXPORTED)\n  png_muldiv           (EXPORTED)\n  png_reciprocal       (EXPORTED)\n  png_gamma_significant(EXPORTED)\n  png_product2         (static)\n  png_reciprocal2      (EXPORTED)\n\n=> exactly 10 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` items.\n\nCRITICAL NOTES:\n  * png.c line 2130 defines the MACROS\n        #define png_fp_add(state, flags) ((state) |= (flags))\n        #define png_fp_set(state, value) ((state) = (value) | ((state) & PNG_FP_STICKY))\n    These SHADOW the static function `png_fp_add` that is already translated in\n    src/png_p2.rs.  You MUST NOT define functions named `png_fp_add` or\n    `png_fp_set`.  Inline them at every use site inside png_check_fp_number:\n        png_fp_add(state, X)   ->  state |= X;\n        png_fp_set(state, V)   ->  state = V | (state & PNG_FP_STICKY);\n  * <math.h>/<float.h>: `crate::pngpriv` provides `floor(x)`, `fabs(x)`,\n    `frexp(x, &mut e)`, `modf(x, &mut d)`, `pow(x,y)` and the constants\n    `DBL_DIG` (15), `DBL_MIN`, `DBL_MAX`, `DBL_MIN_10_EXP` (-307).\n    `frexp`/`modf`/`pow` are `extern \"C\"` so they need `unsafe` (you are in an\n    unsafe fn already).\n  * png_ascii_from_fp is long and delicate: transliterate it EXACTLY,\n    statement by statement, including the `goto` (if any) and all the\n    `#ifdef PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED` (ON) branches. Keep the\n    `char *ascii` pointer arithmetic identical. Do NOT use Rust float\n    formatting.\n  * png_muldiv uses `#ifdef PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED` (ON) -> the\n    `double` implementation.\n  * `png_fixed` and `png_fixed_ITU` take `double fp` -> `f64`.\n  * png_check_IHDR uses `png_warning`/`png_error`/`png_benign_error` — all exist.\n  * `#if PNG_LIBPNG_VER < 10700` is TRUE.\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular NOT src/png.rs, src/png_p1.rs,\nsrc/png_p2.rs, src/png_p4.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-pngp3 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/png_p3.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nTo fully type-check, copy the crate to $TMPDIR, add throwaway stubs for names\nbelonging to png_p4 (png_image_free, png_gamma_correct, png_build_gamma_table,\npng_destroy_gamma_table, png_set_option, png_image_error, png_sRGB_* tables,\npng_gamma_8bit_correct, png_gamma_16bit_correct) and to other not-yet-written\nmodules (png_save_uint_32 from pngwutil.c, ...), build there, fix errors in YOUR\nfile, delete the scratch copy, apply fixes to the real src/png_p3.rs.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/png_p3.rs  -> must be 10.\n\nFINAL REPORT: no_mangle count + symbol names, line count, remaining error lines.","agentId":"ad32ad0bfe3adcbf1","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`src/png_p3.rs` is written and verified.\n\n## Results\n\n**File:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust/src/png_p3.rs` — 948 lines.\n\n**`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` count: 11, not 10.** The task brief said 10, but the function list it gave itself contains 11 EXPORTED entries. I re-counted against `c_src/src/png.c` lines 1961–2999 and confirmed 11 non-`static` functions in range; none of them were already defined in `png_p1.rs`/`png_p2.rs`/elsewhere. Symbols (verified present as `T` in a test-built `libpng.so`):\n\n`png_check_IHDR`, `png_check_fp_number`, `png_check_fp_string`, `png_ascii_from_fp`, `png_ascii_from_fixed`, `png_fixed`, `png_fixed_ITU`, `png_muldiv`, `png_reciprocal`, `png_gamma_significant`, `png_reciprocal2`\n\nPlus one `pub(crate) unsafe fn png_pow10`. `png_product2` is inside `#ifndef PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED`, which is OFF for this build, so it is not compiled (noted in a comment).\n\n**Errors in `src/png_p3.rs`: none.** Zero warnings too. Remaining crate errors are only the two pre-existing ones from unwritten modules (`png_image_free` in png_p4, `png_save_uint_32` in pngwutil). No other file was modified.\n\n## Notes on the tricky parts\n\n- `png_fp_add`/`png_fp_set` macros were inlined at every use site; no functions with those names are defined in this file (the `png_p2.rs` static `png_fp_add` is untouched and unshadowed).\n- The `goto PNG_FP_End` in `png_check_fp_number` became a labeled block `'PNG_FP_End: { ... }`. The C `case A + B:` labels required local `const` aliases since Rust patterns can't hold arithmetic expressions.\n- `png_ascii_from_fp` was transliterated statement-by-statement, keeping `char *ascii` pointer arithmetic (`*ascii = v; ascii = ascii.add(1)` / `ascii = ascii.sub(1)`), the `do…while`, and the `while (exp_b10-- > 0)` post-decrement semantics. No Rust float formatting.\n- `png_ascii_from_fixed`: `(png_uint_32)(-fp)` uses `fp.wrapping_neg()` so `i32::MIN` matches C's practical behavior (and the `num <= 0x80000000` guard).\n- `png_fixed_error` returns `!`, so `png_fixed`/`png_fixed_ITU` diverge in the overflow branch as in C.\n\n## Differential testing against the original C\n\nI compiled verbatim C references for the delicate functions and diffed them against the Rust cdylib (then deleted the scratch copies):\n\n- `png_ascii_from_fp` / `png_ascii_from_fixed`: **801,587 checks, 0 mismatches** — all precisions 0..18, denormals, `1e±300/±310`, `inf`, `5e-324`, `DBL_MAX`, plus ~400k random doubles across exponents −310..310 and ~400k random fixed-point values. Compared the full output buffer, not just the string.\n- `png_check_fp_number` / `png_check_fp_string`: **1,056,381 checks, 0 mismatches** — exhaustive over all strings of length ≤4 from the alphabet `+-.0159Ee <NUL>aZ`, at every `size` and with two initial states, plus 300k random strings including high-bit bytes. Compared return value, final `state`, and final `whereami`.\n- `png_muldiv` / `png_reciprocal` / `png_reciprocal2` / `png_gamma_significant`: **1,804,930 checks, 0 mismatches** — full cross-product of 17 boundary seeds for `muldiv` plus 600k random triples, and 400k random inputs each for the others.\n- `png_check_IHDR`: mechanically diffed all warning/error string literals against the C range — identical text and order, with the `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED` branch taken (the `#else` \"Unknown filter method in IHDR\" omitted) and `Invalid IHDR data` on the error path."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":530870,"totalTokens":154164,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_read_input_tokens":151472,"output_tokens":1522,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1168},"