{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01UDMJ11ESkJM5gyAz2twMuE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libpng C -> Rust translation contract (READ THIS FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tYou are translating one C file (or a range of functions from one C file) of\n4\tlibpng 1.6.59 from `c_src/src/*.c` into a Rust module in `src/`.\n5\t\n6\tThe goal is a **mechanical, line-by-line transliteration** that behaves\n7\t*identically* to the C, not idiomatic Rust. Do NOT restructure, do NOT \"fix\"\n8\tbugs, do NOT change the order of checks, do NOT change error messages.\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Foundation already written (DO NOT MODIFY THESE FILES)\n11\t\n12\t| file | contents |\n13\t|---|---|\n14\t| `src/types.rs` | all `png_*` type aliases, public structs (`png_color`, `png_color_16`, `png_color_8`, `png_sPLT_entry`, `png_sPLT_t`, `png_text`, `png_time`, `png_unknown_chunk`, `png_row_info`, `png_xy`, `png_XYZ`, `png_image`, `png_control`, `png_compression_buffer`, `jmp_buf`), all callback types |\n15\t| `src/pngstruct.rs` | `png_struct` (all fields, same names as pngstruct.h) |\n16\t| `src/pnginfo.rs` | `png_info` (all fields, same names as pnginfo.h) |\n17\t| `src/pngpriv.rs` | every `#define` constant from pngpriv.h / png.h / pnglibconf.h, plus macro-equivalent inline fns |\n18\t| `src/zlib.rs` | `z_stream` + `inflate*`/`deflate*`/`crc32` (zlib API subset), `Z_*` constants |\n19\t| `src/pngerror.rs` | pngerror.c (done) |\n20\t| `src/pngmem.rs` | pngmem.c (done) |\n21\t| `src/pngrio.rs` | pngrio.c (done) |\n22\t| `src/pngwio.rs` | pngwio.c (done) |\n23\t\n24\tRead the files you need before writing code. `src/pngrio.rs`, `src/pngmem.rs`\n25\tand `src/pngerror.rs` show the exact expected style.\n26\t\n27\t## 1. Rules for exported symbols\n28\t\n29\tEvery function that the C file defines **without** `static` must become:\n30\t\n31\t```rust\n32\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n33\tpub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn png_whatever(a: png_structrp, b: c_int) -> c_int { ... }\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t* Use `extern \"C-unwind\"` (NOT `extern \"C\"`) everywhere — the crate relies on\n37\t  unwinding for the simplified-API error path.\n38\t* `static` C functions become `pub(crate) unsafe fn name(...)` (plain Rust ABI)\n39\t  **unless** they are used as a C callback / function pointer stored in a\n40\t  struct, in which case they must also be `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` (but\n41\t  without `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`).\n42\t* Functions declared `PNG_NORETURN` in C (`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`,\n43\t  `png_longjmp`, `png_fixed_error`) return `!` in Rust. Calling them diverges.\n44\t\n45\t## 2. Type mapping\n46\t\n47\t| C | Rust |\n48\t|---|---|\n49\t| `int`, `unsigned int` | `c_int`, `c_uint` |\n50\t| `png_byte` | `png_byte` (= `u8`) |\n51\t| `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` | `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` |\n52\t| `png_uint_32` / `png_int_32` | `png_uint_32` (=`u32`) / `png_int_32` (=`i32`) |\n53\t| `png_fixed_point` | `png_fixed_point` (= `i32`) |\n54\t| `size_t`, `png_alloc_size_t` | `usize`, `png_alloc_size_t` (= `usize`) |\n55\t| `double` | `f64` |\n56\t| `char *` / `const char *` | `png_charp` / `png_const_charp` |\n57\t| `png_structrp`, `png_const_structrp`, `png_structp` | all `*mut png_struct` (aliases exist) |\n58\t| `png_inforp`, `png_const_inforp`, `png_infop` | all `*mut png_info` (aliases exist) |\n59\t| `png_bytep` / `png_const_bytep` | `*mut u8` / `*const u8` |\n60\t| `uInt` (zlib) | `u32` |\n61\t| `voidpf` (zlib) | `*mut c_void` |\n62\t| `FILE *` | `*mut libc::FILE` |\n63\t| function pointer typedefs | the `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(...)>` aliases in `types.rs` |\n64\t\n65\t`const` is dropped on struct pointers (ABI identical), so no casts are needed.\n66\t\n67\t## 3. Idioms\n68\t\n69\t* String literals: `c\"some text\".as_ptr()` produces a `*const c_char`.\n70\t* NULL: `core::ptr::null()` / `core::ptr::null_mut()`.\n71\t* `p != NULL` -> `!p.is_null()`; `p == NULL` -> `p.is_null()`.\n72\t* `fn_ptr != NULL` -> `f.is_some()`; call with `if let Some(f) = (*png_ptr).read_data_fn { f(..) }`.\n73\t* `->` becomes `(*ptr).field`.\n74\t* Pointer arithmetic: `p + n` -> `p.add(n)`, `p - n` -> `p.sub(n)`,\n75\t  `*p++ = v` -> `*p = v; p = p.add(1);`, `*--p = v` -> `p = p.sub(1); *p = v;`.\n76\t* Pointer difference `a - b` -> `(a as usize) - (b as usize)` (or\n77\t  `a.offset_from(b)` when a real element count is wanted).\n78\t* `memcpy`/`memset`/`memmove`/`memcmp`/`strlen`/`strcmp` — use the helpers in\n79\t  `crate::pngpriv` (`memcpy(dst, src, n)` etc., all take `*mut u8`/`*const u8`;\n80\t  cast with `as *mut u8` / `as *const u8`).\n81\t* Arithmetic **must not panic**: C integer arithmetic wraps. Use\n82\t  `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` / `wrapping_mul` when a value could overflow,\n83\t  and be careful with `as` casts (Rust `as` truncates like C).\n84\t* Beware of C integer promotion: `(png_byte)a - (png_byte)b` is computed in\n85\t  `int` in C. Translate as `a as c_int - b as c_int`.\n86\t* Local arrays: `let mut buf: [u8; N] = [0; N];` then `buf.as_mut_ptr()`.\n87\t* `switch` -> `match` (remember C fall-through must be replicated explicitly).\n88\t* `goto` -> restructure with a labelled `loop`/`break` or duplicate the code;\n89\t  keep semantics identical.\n90\t* Do **not** use `Box`, `Vec`, `String` or any `Drop` type for locals in\n91\t  functions that may call `png_error` (a real `longjmp` may fly past them).\n92\t  Use raw pointers + `png_malloc`/`png_free` exactly like the C code.\n93\t\n94\t## 4. Cross-module references and file layout\n95\t\n96\t`src/prelude.rs` re-exports **everything** (all types, all constants, all\n97\tfunctions of every module). So a translated module only needs\n98\t\n99\t```rust\n100\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tand every libpng name is in scope (all libpng symbol names are unique).\n104\t\n105\tThe module for each C file is named after it: `png.c` -> `src/png.rs`,\n106\t`pngrutil.c` -> `src/pngrutil.rs`, etc.\n107\t\n108\t**Large C files are