oth `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL` / `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(N)` macros were inlined verbatim at all 7 use sites (they contain `return`), with the `push_length + 4` sum computed in 32-bit wrapping arithmetic then widened to `usize`, exactly as C promotes it.\n- The C `else if ((keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(...)) != 0)` chain was restructured into a nested `else { let keep = ...; if keep != 0 {...} else if ... }` so the side-effecting call still only happens when neither IHDR nor IEND matched.\n- `case 6`/`default` of the interlace `switch` uses a labelled `loop` + `break 'case6` to reproduce the mid-case `break` out of the switch.\n- Pass tables emitted as private (non-`pub`) `static NAME: [png_byte; 7]` so they cannot collide with the same-named statics that pngrutil/pngrtran will define via the prelude glob.\n- Mode `#define`s (`PNG_READ_SIG_MODE` … `PNG_ERROR_MODE`) are declared as `pub const c_int` here; confirmed via grep they are referenced nowhere else in the C tree.\n- All subtractions/additions on `size_t`/`png_byte`/`png_uint_32` that can wrap in C use `wrapping_*` (e.g. `num_to_check - 4` in `png_push_read_sig`, `PNG_SIZE_MAX - (...)` in `png_push_save_buffer`, `pass++`/`pass--` in `png_read_push_finish_row`).\n- One Rust-parser fix needed: `x as c_int < CONST` had to be parenthesized as `(x as c_int) < CONST`.","usage":{"total_tokens":160207,"tool_uses":37,"duration_ms":469417},"uuid":"9525d6ff-a74c-4a8e-b9bd-25dee8aa1e44","session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204"}
