ly as C promotes it.\n- The C `else if ((keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(...)) != 0)` chain was restructured into a nested `else { let keep = ...; if keep != 0 {...} else if ... }` so the side-effecting call still only happens when neither IHDR nor IEND matched.\n- `case 6`/`default` of the interlace `switch` uses a labelled `loop` + `break 'case6` to reproduce the mid-case `break` out of the switch.\n- Pass tables emitted as private (non-`pub`) `static NAME: [png_byte; 7]` so they cannot collide with the same-named statics that pngrutil/pngrtran will define via the prelude glob.\n- Mode `#define`s (`PNG_READ_SIG_MODE` … `PNG_ERROR_MODE`) are declared as `pub const c_int` here; confirmed via grep they are referenced nowhere else in the C tree.\n- All subtractions/additions on `size_t`/`png_byte`/`png_uint_32` that can wrap in C use `wrapping_*` (e.g. `num_to_check - 4` in `png_push_read_sig`, `PNG_SIZE_MAX - (...)` in `png_push_save_buffer`, `pass++`/`pass--` in `png_read_push_finish_row`).\n- One Rust-parser fix needed: `x as c_int < CONST` had to be parenthesized as `(x as c_int) < CONST`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a7cf644e76fdfb3ef (use SendMessage with to: 'a7cf644e76fdfb3ef', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 161138\ntool_uses: 37\nduration_ms: 469419</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204","uuid":"aad4fa3a-4796-4259-ae8c-d7c3a239a070","timestamp":"2026-08-22T14:49:14.724Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are translating part of libpng 1.6.59 from C to Rust.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — read completely before writing code:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the contract; follow it exactly)\n- src/types.rs, src/pngstruct.rs, src/pnginfo.rs, src/pngpriv.rs, src/zlib.rs\n- src/png_p1.rs and src/pngget.rs (style examples of the expected output)\n\nSTEP 2 — read the EN