ndled_ok` in\n    `crate::pngpriv`.\n\nDo NOT modify any other file. Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-pread cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/pngpread.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nThe crate build currently aborts on unresolved names from not-yet-written\nmodules (pngwutil.c, pngread.c, pngrutil.c, pngrtran.c, pngset.c, pngwrite.c).\nTo fully type-check your own file, copy the crate to $TMPDIR, add throwaway\nstubs for those names there, build, fix the errors in YOUR file, delete the\nscratch copy, and apply the fixes to the real src/pngpread.rs.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/pngpread.rs  -> must be 19.\n\nFINAL REPORT: no_mangle count, line count, remaining error lines + which module\neach missing name belongs to.","agentId":"a7cf644e76fdfb3ef","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only `src/pngpread.rs` was modified. Translation complete.\n\n## Report\n\n**File:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust/src/pngpread.rs`\n\n- **`unsafe(no_mangle)` count: 19** (exactly the required set — verified by `nm` on a stub-linked scratch build that all 19 symbols are actually exported)\n- **Line count: 998**\n\n### Verification\nBuilt a throwaway copy in `$TMPDIR` with stubs for the 13 not-yet-translated names; **that build completed with zero errors and zero warnings in `src/pngpread.rs`** (I also stripped `allow(dead_code)`/`allow(unused_*)` from the scratch `lib.rs` to expose any latent warnings — still none). Scratch copy deleted afterwards.\n\n### Remaining error lines in the real build (all unresolved cross-module names, none are defects in this file)\n\n| line | missing name | belongs to |\n|---|---|---|\n| 190 | `png_read_chunk_header` | pngrutil.c |\n| 245, 252, 287 | `png_handle_chunk` | pngrutil.c |\n| 265 | `png_handle_unknown` | pngrutil.c |\n| 440 | `png_get_uint_31` | pngrutil.c |\n| 442 | `png_crc_read` | pngrutil.c |\n| 516 | `png_crc_finish` | pngrutil.c |\n| 571 | `png_zlib_inflate` | pngrutil.c |\n| 649 | `png_read_filter_row` | pngrutil.c |\n| 673 | `png_do_read_transformations` | **pngrtran.c** |\n| 692 | `png_do_read_interlace` | pngrutil.c |\n| 968 | `png_combine_row` | pngrutil.c |\n\n(Unrelated pre-existing errors elsewhere: `png_save_uint_32` in `png_p1.rs` → pngwutil.c; `png_destroy_write_struct` → pngwrite.c and `png_destroy_read_struct` → pngread.c in `png_p4.rs`.)\n\n### Translation notes\n- Both `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_FULL` / `PNG_PUSH_SAVE_BUFFER_IF_LT(N)` macros were inlined verbatim at all 7 use sites (they contain `return`), with the `push_length + 4` sum computed in 32-bit wrapping arithmetic then widened to `usize`, exactly as C promotes it.\n- The C `else if ((keep = png_chunk_unknown_handling(...)) != 0)` chain was restructured into a nested `else { let keep = ...; if keep != 0 {...} else if ... }` so the side-effecting call still only happens when neither IHDR nor IEND matched.\n- `case 6`/`default` of the interlace `switch` uses a labelled `loop` + `break 'case6` to reproduce the mid-case `break` out of the switch.\n- Pass tables emitted as private (non-`pub`) `static NAME: [png_byte; 7]` so they cannot collide with the same-named statics that pngrutil/pngrtran will define via the prelude glob.\n- Mode `#define`s (`PNG_READ_SIG_MODE` … `PNG_ERROR_MODE`) are declared as `pub const c_int` here; confirmed via grep they are referenced nowhere else in the C tree.\n- All subtractions/additions on `size_t`/`png_byte`/`png_uint_32` that can wrap in C use `wrapping_*` (e.g. `num_to_check - 4` in `png_push_read_sig`, `PNG_SIZE_MAX - (...)` in `png_push_save_buffer`, `pass++`/`pass--` in `png_read_push_finish_row`).\n- One Rust-parser fix needed: `x as c_int < CONST` had to be parenthesized as `(x as c_int) < CONST`."}],"resolvedModel":"glob