{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CYjmY6p2DSv1ajYXjGETC8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# libpng C -> Rust translation contract (READ THIS FIRST)\n2\t\n3\tYou are translating one C file (or a range of functions from one C file) of\n4\tlibpng 1.6.59 from `c_src/src/*.c` into a Rust module in `src/`.\n5\t\n6\tThe goal is a **mechanical, line-by-line transliteration** that behaves\n7\t*identically* to the C, not idiomatic Rust. Do NOT restructure, do NOT \"fix\"\n8\tbugs, do NOT change the order of checks, do NOT change error messages.\n9\t\n10\t## 0. Foundation already written (DO NOT MODIFY THESE FILES)\n11\t\n12\t| file | contents |\n13\t|---|---|\n14\t| `src/types.rs` | all `png_*` type aliases, public structs (`png_color`, `png_color_16`, `png_color_8`, `png_sPLT_entry`, `png_sPLT_t`, `png_text`, `png_time`, `png_unknown_chunk`, `png_row_info`, `png_xy`, `png_XYZ`, `png_image`, `png_control`, `png_compression_buffer`, `jmp_buf`), all callback types |\n15\t| `src/pngstruct.rs` | `png_struct` (all fields, same names as pngstruct.h) |\n16\t| `src/pnginfo.rs` | `png_info` (all fields, same names as pnginfo.h) |\n17\t| `src/pngpriv.rs` | every `#define` constant from pngpriv.h / png.h / pnglibconf.h, plus macro-equivalent inline fns |\n18\t| `src/zlib.rs` | `z_stream` + `inflate*`/`deflate*`/`crc32` (zlib API subset), `Z_*` constants |\n19\t| `src/pngerror.rs` | pngerror.c (done) |\n20\t| `src/pngmem.rs` | pngmem.c (done) |\n21\t| `src/pngrio.rs` | pngrio.c (done) |\n22\t| `src/pngwio.rs` | pngwio.c (done) |\n23\t\n24\tRead the files you need before writing code. `src/pngrio.rs`, `src/pngmem.rs`\n25\tand `src/pngerror.rs` show the exact expected style.\n26\t\n27\t## 1. Rules for exported symbols\n28\t\n29\tEvery function that the C file defines **without** `static` must become:\n30\t\n31\t```rust\n32\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n33\tpub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn png_whatever(a: png_structrp, b: c_int) -> c_int { ... }\n34\t```\n35\t\n36\t* Use `extern \"C-unwind\"` (NOT `extern \"C\"`) everywhere — the crate relies on\n37\t  unwinding for the simplified-API error path.\n38\t* `static` C functions become `pub(crate) unsafe fn name(...)` (plain Rust ABI)\n39\t  **unless** they are used as a C callback / function pointer stored in a\n40\t  struct, in which case they must also be `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` (but\n41\t  without `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`).\n42\t* Functions declared `PNG_NORETURN` in C (`png_error`, `png_chunk_error`,\n43\t  `png_longjmp`, `png_fixed_error`) return `!` in Rust. Calling them diverges.\n44\t\n45\t## 2. Type mapping\n46\t\n47\t| C | Rust |\n48\t|---|---|\n49\t| `int`, `unsigned int` | `c_int`, `c_uint` |\n50\t| `png_byte` | `png_byte` (= `u8`) |\n51\t| `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` | `png_uint_16` / `png_int_16` |\n52\t| `png_uint_32` / `png_int_32` | `png_uint_32` (=`u32`) / `png_int_32` (=`i32`) |\n53\t| `png_fixed_point` | `png_fixed_point` (= `i32`) |\n54\t| `size_t`, `png_alloc_size_t` | `usize`, `png_alloc_size_t` (= `usize`) |\n55\t| `double` | `f64` |\n56\t| `char *` / `const char *` | `png_charp` / `png_const_charp` |\n57\t| `png_structrp`, `png_const_structrp`, `png_structp` | all `*mut png_struct` (aliases exist) |\n58\t| `png_inforp`, `png_const_inforp`, `png_infop` | all `*mut png_info` (aliases exist) |\n59\t| `png_bytep` / `png_const_bytep` | `*mut u8` / `*const u8` |\n60\t| `uInt` (zlib) | `u32` |\n61\t| `voidpf` (zlib) | `*mut c_void` |\n62\t| `FILE *` | `*mut libc::FILE` |\n63\t| function pointer typedefs | the `Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(...)>` aliases in `types.rs` |\n64\t\n65\t`const` is dropped on struct pointers (ABI identical), so no casts are needed.\n66\t\n67\t## 3. Idioms\n68\t\n69\t* String literals: `c\"some text\".as_ptr()` produces a `*const c_char`.\n70\t* NULL: `core::ptr::null()` / `core::ptr::null_mut()`.\n71\t* `p != NULL` -> `!p.is_null()`; `p == NULL` -> `p.is_null()`.\n72\t* `fn_ptr != NULL` -> `f.is_some()`; call with `if let Some(f) = (*png_ptr).read_data_fn { f(..) }`.\n73\t* `->` becomes `(*ptr).field`.\n74\t* Pointer arithmetic: `p + n` -> `p.add(n)`, `p - n` -> `p.sub(n)`,\n75\t  `*p++ = v` -> `*p = v; p = p.add(1);`, `*--p = v` -> `p = p.sub(1); *p = v;`.\n76\t* Pointer difference `a - b` -> `(a as usize) - (b as usize)` (or\n77\t  `a.offset_from(b)` when a real element count is wanted).\n78\t* `memcpy`/`memset`/`memmove`/`memcmp`/`strlen`/`strcmp` — use the helpers in\n79\t  `crate::pngpriv` (`memcpy(dst, src, n)` etc., all take `*mut u8`/`*const u8`;\n80\t  cast with `as *mut u8` / `as *const u8`).\n81\t* Arithmetic **must not panic**: C integer arithmetic wraps. Use\n82\t  `wrapping_add` / `wrapping_sub` / `wrapping_mul` when a value could overflow,\n83\t  and be careful with `as` casts (Rust `as` truncates like C).\n84\t* Beware of C integer promotion: `(png_byte)a - (png_byte)b` is computed in\n85\t  `int` in C. Translate as `a as c_int - b as c_int`.\n86\t* Local arrays: `let mut buf: [u8; N] = [0; N];` then `buf.as_mut_ptr()`.\n87\t* `switch` -> `match` (remember C fall-through must be replicated explicitly).\n88\t* `goto` -> restructure with a labelled `loop`/`break` or duplicate the code;\n89\t  keep semantics identical.\n90\t* Do **not** use `Box`, `Vec`, `String` or any `Drop` type for locals in\n91\t  functions that may call `png_error` (a real `longjmp` may fly past them).\n92\t  Use raw pointers + `png_malloc`/`png_free` exactly like the C code.\n93\t\n94\t## 4. Cross-module references and file layout\n95\t\n96\t`src/prelude.rs` re-exports **everything** (all types, all constants, all\n97\tfunctions of every module). So a translated module only needs\n98\t\n99\t```rust\n100\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n101\t```\n102\t\n103\tand every libpng name is in scope (all libpng symbol names are unique).\n104\t\n105\tThe module for each C file is named after it: `png.c` -> `src/png.rs`,\n106\t`pngrutil.c` -> `src/pngrutil.rs`, etc.\n107\t\n108\t**Large C files are split into \"part\" files** that are textually included into\n109\tthe module by the wrapper (already created), e.g. `src/png.rs` contains\n110\t\n111\t```rust\n112\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n113\tinclude!(\"png_p1.rs\");\n114\tinclude!(\"png_p2.rs\");\n115\tinclude!(\"png_p3.rs\");\n116\tinclude!(\"png_p4.rs\");\n117\t```\n118\t\n119\tIf you are assigned a part file (`src/<name>_pN.rs`):\n120\t\n121\t* Write ONLY item definitions (functions, `static`s, `struct`s, `const`s,\n122\t  optionally extra `use` statements). Everything ends up in the same module, so\n123\t  `static` helpers, structs and private fns defined in one part are directly\n124\t  visible to the others — no `pub` / `use` needed between parts.\n125\t* The first line must be a normal `//` comment, **never** a `//!` inner doc\n126\t  comment (illegal in an included file).\n127\t* Do not add `#![...]` inner attributes.\n128\t* Do not touch the wrapper `src/<name>.rs` or any other part file.\n129\t\n130\tIf you are assigned a whole module file (`src/<name>.rs`), start it with\n131\t\n132\t```rust\n133\t//! Translated from c_src/src/<name>.c\n134\t\n135\tuse crate::prelude::*;\n136\t```\n137\t\n138\t### `PNG_WARNING_PARAMETERS(p)` / `png_warning_parameters`\n139\t\n140\t`png_warning_parameters p;` becomes\n141\t\n142\t```rust\n143\tlet mut p: [[c_char; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT] =\n144\t    [[0; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_SIZE]; PNG_WARNING_PARAMETER_COUNT];\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\tand is passed as `p.as_mut_ptr()` (type `*mut [c_char; 32]`).\n148\t\n149\t### zlib\n150\t\n151\t`png_ptr->zstream` is a `crate::zlib::z_stream` with fields `next_in`\n152\t(`*const u8`), `avail_in` (`u32`), `next_out` (`*mut u8`), `avail_out` (`u32`),\n153\t`msg` (`*const c_char`), `zalloc`, `zfree`, `opaque`, `state`, `total_in`,\n154\t`total_out`, `adler`, `data_type`, `reserved`.\n155\t\n156\tCall the zlib functions as free functions:\n157\t`inflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, wb)`, `inflate(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, flush)`,\n158\t`inflateReset2`, `inflateReset`, `inflateValidate`, `inflateEnd`,\n159\t`deflateInit2(&mut (*png_ptr).zstream, level, method, wb, memLevel, strategy)`,\n160\t`deflate`, `deflateReset`, `deflateEnd`, `crc32(crc, ptr, len)`.\n161\t`ZLIB_VERNUM` is 0x12b0 (>= 0x1240), so compile the \"modern zlib\" branches.\n162\t`PNGZ_MSG_CAST(s)` is just `s`; `PNGZ_INPUT_CAST(b)` is just `b`.\n163\t`ZLIB_IO_MAX` is `crate::zlib::ZLIB_IO_MAX` (`u32::MAX`).\n164\t\n165\t### `png_debug*`\n166\t\n167\tAll `png_debug`, `png_debug1`, `png_debug2` calls are no-ops — just delete them.\n168\t\n169\t### `PNG_UNUSED(x)`\n170\t\n171\tDelete.\n172\t\n173\t## 5. Which `#ifdef`s are ON\n174\t\n175\tTreat these as **defined** (see `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h` for the full list —\n176\tessentially everything except the CPU-specific optimizations):\n177\t\n178\t* All `PNG_READ_*`, `PNG_WRITE_*`, chunk support, `PNG_SETJMP_SUPPORTED`,\n179\t  `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`,\n180\t  `PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_POINT_SUPPORTED`,\n181\t  `PNG_FIXED_POINT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FLOATING_ARITHMETIC_SUPPORTED`,\n182\t  `PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONSOLE_IO_SUPPORTED`,\n183\t  `PNG_PROGRESSIVE_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SEQUENTIAL_READ_SUPPORTED`,\n184\t  `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_READ_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED`,\n185\t  `PNG_COLORSPACE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GAMMA_SUPPORTED`,\n186\t  `PNG_BENIGN_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_BENIGN_READ_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`,\n187\t  `PNG_WARNINGS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ERROR_TEXT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_TEXT_SUPPORTED`,\n188\t  `PNG_TIME_RFC1123_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_CONVERT_tIME_SUPPORTED`,\n189\t  `PNG_EASY_ACCESS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_INCH_CONVERSIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n190\t  `PNG_IO_STATE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_MNG_FEATURES_SUPPORTED`,\n191\t  `PNG_SET_OPTION_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_UNKNOWN_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED` (+ READ/WRITE/SET/STORE/SAVE variants),\n192\t  `PNG_USER_CHUNKS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_HANDLE_AS_UNKNOWN_SUPPORTED`,\n193\t  `PNG_CHECK_FOR_INVALID_INDEX_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_GET_PALETTE_MAX_SUPPORTED`,\n194\t  `PNG_INFO_IMAGE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_POINTER_INDEXING_SUPPORTED`,\n195\t  `PNG_16BIT_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_ALIGNED_MEMORY_SUPPORTED`,\n196\t  `PNG_BUILD_GRAYSCALE_PALETTE_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_COMPOSITE_NODIV_SUPPORTED`,\n197\t  `PNG_USE_READ_MACROS`, `PNG_WRITE_OPTIMIZE_CMF_SUPPORTED`,\n198\t  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n199\t  `PNG_WRITE_CUSTOMIZE_ZTXT_COMPRESSION_SUPPORTED`,\n200\t  `PNG_WRITE_WEIGHTED_FILTER_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_WRITE_FILTER_SUPPORTED`,\n201\t  `PNG_WRITE_FLUSH_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FORMAT_BGR_SUPPORTED`,\n202\t  `PNG_FORMAT_AFIRST_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_SIMPLIFIED_*_BGR/AFIRST/STDIO_SUPPORTED`,\n203\t  `PNG_SAVE_INT_32_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_READ_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`,\n204\t  `PNG_WRITE_INT_FUNCTIONS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_USER_TRANSFORM_*`.\n205\t\n206\tTreat these as **NOT defined** (omit the code entirely):\n207\t\n208\t* `PNG_ERROR_NUMBERS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED`,\n209\t  `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED`, `PNG_FIXED_POINT_MACRO_SUPPORTED`,\n210\t  `PNG_MAX_MALLOC_64K`, `PNG_ARM_NEON_*`, `PNG_MIPS_*`, `PNG_POWERPC_*`,\n211\t  `PNG_LOONGARCH_*`, `PNG_INTEL_SSE`, `PNG_RISCV_*`, `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS`,\n212\t  `PNG_ARM_NEON_IMPLEMENTATION`, `PNG_RISCV_RVV_IMPLEMENTATION`,\n213\t  `PNG_USER_CONFIG`, `PNG_PREFIX`, `PNG_READ_QUANTIZE_SUPPORTED` is **ON**,\n214\t  `PNG_READ_OPT_PLTE_SUPPORTED` is **ON**.\n215\t* `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is **false** (`PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_BASE_TYPE` == BETA == 2\n216\t  which is `< PNG_LIBPNG_BUILD_RC` == 3), so inside\n217\t  `#if PNG_RELEASE_BUILD ... #else ... #endif` you must take the **`#else`**\n218\t  branch, and `#if !PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` code IS compiled.\n219\t* `PNG_LIBPNG_VER < 10700` is **true**.\n220\t* `PNG_ARM_NEON_OPT`, `PNG_INTEL_SSE_IMPLEMENTATION`, etc. are all `0`.\n221\t\n222\t## 6. Verification\n223\t\n224\tAfter writing the file, run\n225\t\n226\t```\n227\tcargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | tail -40\n228\t```\n229\t\n230\tOther modules may not exist yet, so unresolved-import errors from *other*\n231\tmodules are expected; make sure there are **no errors in your own file**\n232\t(you can check with `cargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | grep -c \"src/YOURFILE.rs\"`).\n233\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014qhZo7zAesUDwbQjA6poJ2","session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204","uuid":"02cc74cb-07c8-4760-b721-f0bbadd8eef5","timestamp":"2026-08-22T15:11:03.202Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pngwutil.c part 2"}
