{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X6KnDu7gqYYSKjDy35C8mF","type":"tool_result","content":"620\t * The basic idea here is to go through the row with a source\n621\t * pointer and a destination pointer (sp and dp), and copy the\n622\t * correct pixels for the pass.  As the row gets compacted,\n623\t * sp will always be >= dp, so we should never overwrite anything.\n624\t * See the default: case for the easiest code to understand.\n625\t */\n626\t#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\n627\tpub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn png_do_write_interlace(\n628\t    row_info: png_row_infop,\n629\t    row: png_bytep,\n630\t    pass: c_int,\n631\t) {\n632\t    /* We don't have to do anything on the last pass (6) */\n633\t    if pass < 6 {\n634\t        /* Each pixel depth is handled separately */\n635\t        match (*row_info).pixel_depth {\n636\t            1 => {\n637\t                let mut sp: png_bytep;\n638\t                let mut dp: png_bytep;\n639\t                let mut shift: c_uint;"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011eMhdy8k1wcxNQyPrT2GvV","session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204","uuid":"b54135fa-644c-409f-9b14-fffc5e29c9d5","timestamp":"2026-08-22T15:33:27.944Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pngwrite.c part 2"}
