the real build (all outside my file)\n\n| Missing name | Referenced from | Belongs to |\n|---|---|---|\n| `png_destroy_read_struct` | `src/png_p4.rs:771` | pngread.c |\n| `png_read_chunk_header` | `src/pngpread.rs:190` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_handle_chunk` (×3) | `src/pngpread.rs:245,252,287` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_handle_unknown` | `src/pngpread.rs:265` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_get_uint_31` | `src/pngpread.rs:440` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_crc_read` | `src/pngpread.rs:442` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_crc_finish` | `src/pngpread.rs:516` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_zlib_inflate` | `src/pngpread.rs:571` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_read_filter_row` | `src/pngpread.rs:649` | pngrutil.c |\n| `png_do_read_transformations` | `src/pngpread.rs:673` | pngrtran.c |\n| `png_do_read_interlace` | `src/pngpread.rs:692` | pngrtran.c |\n| `png_combine_row` | `src/pngpread.rs:968` | pngrtran.c |\n\n## Key translation findings\n\n- **No `setjmp` in this range.** `PNG_USER_MEM_SUPPORTED` is on, so the `#ifdef` in the C makes `png_create_write_struct` a pure one-line forwarder to `png_create_write_struct_2`, and the latter has no `setjmp`/`png_jmpbuf` at all. No `catch_unwind`/longjmp-shim machinery was needed (unlike `png_create_png_struct` in `png_p1.rs`), so no marker struct was added.\n- **Two config branches omitted per the guide:** `PNG_BENIGN_WRITE_ERRORS_SUPPORTED` is off (so `flags |= PNG_FLAG_BENIGN_ERRORS_WARN` is not emitted) and `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is false (so `flags |= PNG_FLAG_APP_WARNINGS_WARN` is not emitted). Both are documented with comments at the site.\n- **`png_set_filter` C fall-through replicated explicitly:** cases `5|6|7` call `png_app_error` and then fall through into the `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE` body, so that arm sets `do_filter = PNG_FILTER_NONE` inline rather than relying on Rust match semantics.\n- **`png_write_destroy`** does *not* call any gamma-table teardown (that is read-side only); it is `deflateEnd` → `png_free_buffer_list` → `row_buf` → `prev_row`/`try_row`/`tst_row` → `chunk_list` → `trans_alpha` → `palette`, in that exact order.\n- **All `#if !defined(PNG_WRITE_x_SUPPORTED) && defined(PNG_READ_x_SUPPORTED)` warning blocks in `png_write_row` are dead** — I confirmed against `c_src/include/pnglibconf.h` that INVERT, FILLER, PACKSWAP, PACK, SHIFT, BGR and SWAP write support are all defined, so none of those seven `png_warning` calls compile.\n- **Integer-promotion care:** `png_do_write_intrapixel` computes the 8-bit deltas via `as c_int` + `wrapping_sub` before truncating, and the 16-bit path builds `s0/s1/s2` as `(byte as c_int) << 8` cast to `png_uint_32` then masks `& 0xffff`, matching C's `int`-then-`unsigned` conversions.\n\n## Independent symbol check\n\nI generated the C symbol table for `pngwrite.c.o` and ran the repo's `./check_syms.sh pngwrite`. The only diff is the three functions that belong to **part 3** (`png_image_write_to_file`, `png_image_write_to_memory`, `png_image_write_to_stdio`). All 24 of my exported names match the C object file exactly — 5 (p1) + 24 (p2) + 3 (p3) = the 32 symbols the C emits."}],"resolvedModel":"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]","totalDurationMs":365596,"totalTokens":140482,"totalToolUseCount":39,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1348,"cache_read_input_tokens":137400,"output_tokens":1732,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1348},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":15,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":23,"editFileCount":1,"linesAdded":969,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
