          `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(png_structp, png_bytep, usize)`)\n  image_memory_flush        (static PNGCBAPI; a `png_flush_ptr` callback)\n  png_image_write_memory    (static; png_safe_execute callback)\n  png_image_write_to_memory (EXPORTED)\n  png_image_write_to_stdio  (EXPORTED)\n  png_image_write_to_file   (EXPORTED)\n\n=> exactly 3 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` items:\n  png_image_write_to_memory, png_image_write_to_stdio, png_image_write_to_file\n\nNOTES:\n  * `png_safe_execute(image, function, arg)` has the Rust signature\n    `(image: png_imagep, function: Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(png_voidp) -> c_int>, arg: png_voidp) -> c_int`\n    so call it as `png_safe_execute(image, Some(png_image_write_main), display_ptr)`.\n  * `png_control` in this port has a `bitfields: c_uint` instead of the C\n    bitfields; use the accessors `set_for_write(1)`, `for_write()`,\n    `set_owned_file(1)`, `owned_file()` (see src/types.rs).\n    `error_buf` is `png_voidp`.\n  * C code that does `memset(&control, 0, sizeof control)` -> build the struct\n    with `core::mem::zeroed()`.\n  * `png_control_jmp_buf(...)` / `setjmp` do NOT appear in this range (they are\n    inside png_safe_execute). If you find any `setjmp` usage, mirror what\n    src/pngerror.rs does (catch_unwind) and explain it.\n  * FILE handling: `libc::fopen`, `libc::fclose`, `libc::fflush`, `libc::ferror`,\n    `libc::FILE`, `libc::fwrite`.\n  * PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_SUPPORTED, PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_STDIO_SUPPORTED,\n    PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_BGR_SUPPORTED, PNG_SIMPLIFIED_WRITE_AFIRST_SUPPORTED,\n    PNG_WRITE_16BIT_SUPPORTED, PNG_STDIO_SUPPORTED are all ON.\n  * `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(linear)` is defined in src/png_p4.rs as\n    `PNG_sRGB_FROM_LINEAR(linear: png_uint_32) -> png_byte` — use it.\n    `png_sRGB_table`, `png_sRGB_base`, `png_sRGB_delta` are exported statics\n    there; index them like `png_sRGB_table[i as usize]`.\n  * `PNG_IMAGE_*` helper macros are inline fns in src/pngpriv.rs\n    (PNG_IMAGE_PIXEL_CHANNELS, PNG_IMAGE_SAMPLE_CHANNELS, ...). Row-stride /\n    buffer-size expressions that the C writes inline must be transliterated\n    with the same operand types (watch for `ptrdiff_t` row_stride being\n    negative: keep it `isize`/`c_long` as in the C).\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular NOT src/pngwrite.rs,\nsrc/pngwrite_p1.rs, src/pngwrite_p2.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-wr3 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/pngwrite_p3.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nThe crate build currently aborts on unresolved names from not-yet-written\nmodules (pngread.c, pngrtran.c, pngrutil.c). To fully type-check your own file,\ncopy the crate to $TMPDIR, add throwaway stubs for those names there, build, fix\nthe errors in YOUR file, delete the scratch copy, and apply the fixes to the\nreal src/pngwrite_p3.rs.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/pngwrite_p3.rs  -> must be 3.\n\nFINAL REPORT: no_mangle count, line count, remaining error lines + which module\neach missing name belongs to."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01KwQ4AoEtYTdMDJfcJgHLGB","session_id":"a9a0a7d5-d080-4cce-a91d-7cd01f6e0204","uuid":"958efc1c-e34a-4921-b725-49326361b695","timestamp":"2026-08-22T15:37:53.944Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate pngwrite.c part 3"}
