ib_inflate           (EXPORTED)\n  png_inflate                (static)\n  png_decompress_chunk       (static)\n  png_inflate_read           (static)\n\n=> exactly 9 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` items:\n  png_get_uint_31, png_get_uint_32, png_get_int_32, png_get_uint_16,\n  png_read_sig, png_read_chunk_header, png_crc_read, png_crc_finish,\n  png_zlib_inflate\n\nCRITICAL NOTES:\n  * Inside the library `png_get_uint_32(buf)` etc. are MACROS\n    (PNG_USE_READ_MACROS): whenever the C *calls* them, use\n    `PNG_get_uint_32(buf)` / `PNG_get_uint_16(buf)` / `PNG_get_int_32(buf)`\n    from `crate::pngpriv`.  The exported *functions* you define here must\n    return exactly the same values (the C bodies just wrap the macros).\n  * ZLIB: `ZLIB_VERNUM` is >= 0x1240 so compile the \"modern zlib\" branches\n    (`inflateReset2`, `inflateInit2`, `png_zlib_inflate`, `zstream_start`).\n    `PNG_DISABLE_ADLER32_CHECK_SUPPORTED` is NOT defined, so the\n    `inflateValidate` call is NOT compiled.\n    `PNG_SET_OPTION_SUPPORTED` IS defined and `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW`\n    IS defined (png.h:3462, value 2), so in `png_inflate_claim` the\n    `#if defined(PNG_SET_OPTION_SUPPORTED) && defined(PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW)`\n    block IS compiled (window_bits stays 0 unless the option is ON, and\n    `png_ptr->zstream_start` is set to 1 in the else branch).\n    Use `crate::zlib::{inflate, inflateInit2, inflateReset2, inflateEnd,\n    Z_OK, Z_STREAM_END, Z_STREAM_ERROR, Z_DATA_ERROR, Z_BUF_ERROR,\n    Z_NO_FLUSH, Z_SYNC_FLUSH, Z_FINISH, ZLIB_IO_MAX}`.\n    `PNGZ_MSG_CAST(s)` is `s`; `PNGZ_INPUT_CAST(b)` is `b`.\n    `png_ptr->zstream.msg = \"invalid window size (libpng)\"` ->\n    `(*png_ptr).zstream.msg = c\"invalid window size (libpng)\".as_ptr();`\n  * `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is FALSE: in `png_inflate_claim` take the `#else`\n    branch (`png_chunk_error(png_ptr, msg)`), NOT the warning-recovery branch.\n  * `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` expands to `(*png_ptr).user_chunk_malloc_max`\n    (PNG_SET_USER_LIMITS_SUPPORTED is on).\n  * `PNG_INFLATE(pp, flush)` -> `png_zlib_inflate(pp, flush)`.\n  * `PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE` is 1024 (crate::pngpriv).\n  * `Byte local_buffer[PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE]` -> `let mut local_buffer: [png_byte; PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE] = [0; PNG_INFLATE_BUF_SIZE];`\n    NOTE it is declared INSIDE the do/while loop in C; keep it inside the loop\n    body in Rust too (its address is taken and stored in zstream.next_out).\n  * `png_ptr->crc` is u32; `crc32(crc: u64, buf: *const u8, len: u32) -> u64`\n    (crate::zlib).\n  * `png_calculate_crc`, `png_read_data`, `png_error`, `png_chunk_error`,\n    `png_chunk_warning`, `png_chunk_benign_error`, `png_benign_error`,\n    `png_warning`, `png_malloc_base`, `png_free`, `png_zstream_error`,\n    `png_safecat`, `PNG_STRING_FROM_CHUNK`, `PNG_CHUNK_NAME_VALID`-style helpers\n    already exist (PNG_CHUNK_ANCILLARY / PNG_CHUNK_CRITICAL /\n    PNG_CHUNK_RESERVED / PNG_CHUNK_PRIVATE / PNG_CHUNK_SAFE_TO_COPY are inline\n    fns in crate::pngpriv; `PNG_CN_VALID_*` are not — inline them yourself).\n  * `png_ptr->IDAT_read_size` is a u32.\n  * `png_ptr->read_buffer_size` is `png_alloc_size_t` (usize).\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular NOT src/pngrutil.rs or the other\npngrutil_p*.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-ru1 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/pngrutil_p1.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nThe crate build currently aborts on unresolved names from not-yet-written\nmodules (pngread.c, pngrtran.c, pngrutil parts 2-5). To fully type-check your\nown file, copy the crate to $TMPDIR, add throwaway stubs for those names there,\nbuild, fix the errors in YOUR file, delete the scratch copy, and apply the fixes\nto the real src/pngrutil_p1.rs.\nAlso run: grep -c \"unsafe(no_mangle)\" src/pngru