e not in the assigned function list but *are* in my line range, so I translated them here (matching the `pngwutil_p1.rs` precedent). **Later parts must not redefine these** or the build will get \"defined multiple times\":\n\n- `const LZ77Min: png_uint_32 = 2 + 5 + 4;` (pngrutil.c:23 — used at C line 1353, i.e. part 2)\n- `static png_pass_start / png_pass_inc / png_pass_ystart / png_pass_yinc: [png_byte; 7]` (pngrutil.c:29-35 — used at C lines 3719+/4381+, i.e. part 4/5)\n\nOther things later parts get for free from part 1: `check_chunk_name`, `png_crc_error`, `png_crc_finish_critical`, `png_read_buffer`, `png_inflate_claim`, `png_inflate`, `png_decompress_chunk`, `png_inflate_read` (all `pub(crate) unsafe fn`).\n\n## Translation decisions worth recording\n\n- `png_get_uint_32`/`_16`/`_int_32` are defined as exported functions with the C bodies, but every *internal call site* uses the `crate::pngpriv` macro equivalents (`PNG_get_uint_32`, etc.) — used in `png_get_uint_31`, `png_get_int_32`, `png_crc_error`.\n- `png_inflate_claim` takes the `#else` (non-release) branch → `png_chunk_error(png_ptr, msg)`; `window_bits` starts at 0 and the `PNG_MAXIMUM_INFLATE_WINDOW` block is compiled (sets `zstream_start` to 0 or 1); `inflateValidate` omitted; `png_safecat(msg, 64, 4, \" using zstream\")`.\n- `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` inlined as `(*png_ptr).user_chunk_malloc_max`; `PNG_INFLATE(pp, flush)` inlined as `png_zlib_inflate(pp, flush)`.\n- `local_buffer` / `tmpbuf` stay declared inside the loop bodies (as in C); the Rust versions are zero-initialized, which is a benign difference since they are write-only output buffers.\n- C integer-promotion rules were preserved at the mixed-width comparisons, notably `avail_out < avail` and `avail > *out_size` (u32 widened to `png_alloc_size_t`) vs. `avail_in < avail` and `read_size > *chunk_bytes` (both u32, no widening), and `limit >= prefix_size + (terminate != 0)` (computed in u32, then widened).","usage":{"total_tokens":149971,"tool_u