se profile` build — so the file is fully type-checked, not just resolution-checked. Scratch copy deleted.\n- No other file was touched.\n\n## Remaining crate-level error lines (all in *other* modules, from not-yet-written parts)\n| error line | missing name | owning module |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/png_p4.rs:771` | `png_destroy_read_struct` | `pngread` (pngread_p*.rs) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:245,252,287` | `png_handle_chunk` | `pngrutil` (a later `pngrutil_p*.rs`) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:265` | `png_handle_unknown` | `pngrutil` (a later `pngrutil_p*.rs`) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:649` | `png_read_filter_row` | `pngrutil` (a later `pngrutil_p*.rs`) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:673` | `png_do_read_transformations` | `pngrtran` (pngrtran_p*.rs) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:692` | `png_do_read_interlace` | `pngrtran` (pngrtran_p*.rs) |\n| `src/pngpread.rs:968` | `png_combine_row` | `pngrtran` (pngrtran_p*.rs) |\n\n## Translation notes worth flagging\n- The task brief said `png_handle_sPLT` uses `png_malloc_array`/`png_realloc_array`/`png_chunk_report`; the actual C at lines 1550-1680 uses `png_malloc_warn` + `png_warning` + `png_free` + `png_set_sPLT`. I followed the C.\n- `png_file_add_chunk` does not appear in this range. `png_has_chunk(png_ptr, X)` was inlined as `((*png_ptr).chunks & png_chunk_flag_from_index(PNG_INDEX_X)) != 0` for tRNS/bKGD (PLTE), mDCV (cHRM), cICP (sRGB).\n- `1U << png_ptr->bit_depth` in PLTE is translated as `1u32.wrapping_shl(...)` so it can never panic in a debug build (C would be UB for bit_depth >= 32, which `png_set_IHDR` already rules out).\n- `return errmsg != NULL ? handled_error : handled_error;` (PLTE) was kept verbatim as an `if`/`else` both yielding `handled_error`, matching the C's deliberate anti-unused-variable idiom.\n- `PNG_UNUSED(...)`, `png_debug*`, and the `#define png_handle_IDAT NULL` line were dropped/commented per the guide.","usage":{"total_tokens":144018,"tool_uses":31,"duration_ms":405281},"uuid":"4a252932-7bfa-4cf8-9cc0-6a8a9f9f3adb","sess