estamp":"2026-08-22T16:01:39.556Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are translating part of libpng 1.6.59 from C to Rust.\n\nWorking directory: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust\n\nSTEP 1 — read completely before writing code:\n- TRANSLATION_GUIDE.md   (the contract; follow it exactly)\n- src/types.rs, src/pngstruct.rs, src/pnginfo.rs, src/pngpriv.rs, src/zlib.rs\n- src/pngrutil_p1.rs  (already-translated sibling part of the SAME module. It\n  provides `check_chunk_name`, `png_crc_error`, `png_crc_finish_critical`,\n  `png_read_buffer`, `png_inflate_claim`, `png_inflate`,\n  `png_decompress_chunk`, `png_inflate_read`, `const LZ77Min`, and the\n  `png_pass_start`/`png_pass_inc`/`png_pass_ystart`/`png_pass_yinc` tables.\n  DO NOT redefine any of them.)\n- src/pngset_p1.rs (the png_set_* functions these handlers call)\n- src/pngrutil.rs (the wrapper that `include!`s your file)\n\nSTEP 2 — read lines 901..1686 of c_src/src/pngrutil.c.\n\nSTEP 3 — write the translation of THAT RANGE ONLY into src/pngrutil_p2.rs.\nIt is `include!`d into module `crate::pngrutil`, so:\n  * first line must be a plain `//` comment (never `//!`)\n  * no `#![...]` inner attributes\n\nContents of this range (in order) — ALL of them are `static` in C, so NONE of\nthem gets `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`; they all become `pub(crate) unsafe fn`:\n  png_handle_IHDR, png_handle_PLTE, png_handle_IEND, png_handle_gAMA,\n  png_handle_sBIT, png_get_int_32_checked, png_handle_cHRM, png_handle_sRGB,\n  png_handle_iCCP, png_handle_sPLT\n\n=> exactly 0 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` items in this file.\n\nAll the `png_handle_*` functions have the C signature\n`static png_handle_result_code png_handle_XXXX(png_structrp png_ptr,\n png_inforp info_ptr, png_uint_32 length)`.\n`png_handle_result_code` is a C enum; in this port it is a `c_int` and the\nenumerators are the constants `handled_error`, `handled_discarded`,\n`handled_saved`, `handled_ok` in `crate::pngpriv`.  So write\n`pub(crate) unsafe fn png_handle_IHDR(png_ptr: png_structrp, info_ptr: png_inforp, length: png_uint_32) -> c_int`.\n\nNOTES:\n  * `png_get_uint_32(buf)` / `png_get_uint_16(buf)` / `png_get_int_32(buf)` are\n    MACROS inside the library: call `PNG_get_uint_32(buf)` etc. from\n    `crate::pngpriv`.\n  * `png_get_uint_31(png_ptr, buf)` IS a real function (pngrutil_p1.rs).\n  * `png_chunk_max(png_ptr)` -> `(*png_ptr).user_chunk_malloc_max`.\n  * `PNG_RELEASE_BUILD` is FALSE.\n  * All chunk read support macros are ON (READ_gAMA, READ_sBIT, READ_cHRM,\n    READ_sRGB, READ_iCCP, READ_sPLT, READ_OPT_PLTE, COLORSPACE, GAMMA, ...).\n  * `png_handle_iCCP` uses `png_icc_check_length` / `png_icc_check_header` /\n    `png_icc_check_tag_table` (src/png_p2.rs) and\n    `png_decompress_chunk`/`png_inflate_read` from pngrutil_p1.rs, plus\n    `png_ptr->zstream.msg`.\n  * `png_handle_sPLT` uses `png_malloc_array`, `png_realloc_array`, `png_free`,\n    `png_chunk_report`.\n  * `png_handle_IHDR` calls `png_check_IHDR`? — read the C; it calls\n    `png_set_IHDR`/`png_check_IHDR` as written. Also sets `png_ptr->rowbytes`\n    via `PNG_ROWBYTES`.\n  * `png_file_add_chunk(png_ptr, PNG_INDEX_xxxx)` -> inline it as\n    `(*png_ptr).chunks |= png_chunk_flag_from_index(PNG_INDEX_xxxx);`\n    `png_file_has_chunk(png_ptr, i)` -> `((*png_ptr).chunks & png_chunk_flag_from_index(i)) != 0`\n    `png_has_chunk(png_ptr, cHNK)` -> same with `PNG_INDEX_cHNK`.\n  * `PNG_WARNING_PARAMETERS(p)` -> see TRANSLATION_GUIDE section 4.\n\nDo NOT modify any other file (in particular NOT src/pngrutil.rs or the other\npngrutil_p*.rs). Do NOT modify anything under c_src/.\n\nSTEP 4 — verify:\n  cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-bpUWKO/translated_rust && CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/tgt-ru2 cargo build --release --offline --message-format=short 2>&1 | grep \"^src/pngrutil_p2.rs\" | grep -v \": warning\" | head -60\nThe crate build currently aborts on unresolved names from not-yet-writt