al`, `check_chunk_name`, `LZ77Min` and the\n  `png_pass_start`/`png_pass_inc`/`png_pass_ystart`/`png_pass_yinc` tables.\n  DO NOT redefine any of them.)\n- src/pngrutil.rs (the wrapper that `include!`s your file)\n\nSTEP 2 — read lines 3711..4684 of c_src/src/pngrutil.c.\n\nSTEP 3 — write the translation of THAT RANGE ONLY into src/pngrutil_p5.rs.\nIt is `include!`d into module `crate::pngrutil`, so:\n  * first line must be a plain `//` comment (never `//!`)\n  * no `#![...]` inner attributes\n\nContents of this range (in order):\n  png_do_read_interlace                     (EXPORTED)\n  png_read_filter_row_sub                   (static)\n  png_read_filter_row_up                    (static)\n  png_read_filter_row_avg                   (static)\n  png_read_filter_row_paeth_1byte_pixel     (static)\n  png_read_filter_row_paeth_multibyte_pixel (static)\n  png_init_filter_functions                 (static)\n  png_read_filter_row                       (EXPORTED)\n  png_read_IDAT_data                        (EXPORTED)\n  png_read_finish_IDAT                      (EXPORTED)\n  png_read_finish_row                       (EXPORTED)\n  png_read_start_row                        (EXPORTED)\n\n=> exactly 6 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn` items:\n  png_do_read_interlace, png_read_filter_row, png_read_IDAT_data,\n  png_read_finish_IDAT, png_read_finish_row, png_read_start_row\n\nCRITICAL NOTES:\n  * The five `png_read_filter_row_*` statics are stored into\n    `png_ptr->read_filter[]`, whose Rust type is\n    `[Option<unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(png_row_infop, png_bytep, png_const_bytep)>; 4]`\n    (see `png_read_filter_fn` in src/pngstruct.rs). So define them as\n    `unsafe extern \"C-unwind\" fn(row_info: png_row_infop, row: png_bytep, prev_row: png_const_bytep)`\n    WITHOUT `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`, and assign `Some(png_read_filter_row_sub)` etc.\n  * `PNG_FILTER_OPTIMIZATIONS` is NOT defined and all the CPU-specific\n    optimizations are OFF, so `png